  "conclusions": [
    "The old six-stage assertion first fails at stage 6; stages 1-5 have no asserted-row mismatch.",
    "Immediately after the public Qt resize and before stage-6 output, the core keeps B/C/D source rows and the display page reflows B to row 8 and CD to row 11; the native grid at that instant is not observed (child ACK comes only after its stage-6 write).",
    "At stage 6, native ConPTY has reflowed the old rows; native row 8 matches the display row 8, while native row 11/12 differ by the CUP 12;1 coordinate layer and core retains the old source rows. No transport bytes move/erase B/C/D.",
    "This is a native-grid vs retained-source/display coordinate difference, not evidence that the parser ignored reflow bytes. It does not decide which product policy should win, does not change the old --resize failure, and does not use the WindTerm write endpoint as this oracle."
